    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 0. Sheet Setup (Idempotent)\nBefore processing, the workflow ensures the destination Google Sheet exists. \"Search spreadsheet\" looks for a spreadsheet named \"Gmail Email Processing Log\"; if found it is reused, otherwise \"Create spreadsheet\" creates it with the \"Gmail Email Processing Log\" tab. \"Set Spreadsheet ID\" stores the resulting ID (which both Append nodes reference). The Append nodes use auto-map mode, so on an empty sheet they write the 9 field names as the header row automatically before adding data, and reuse the existing header row afterwards — no separate header-writing step is needed.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "d7293e28-be83-48b3-8e01-01935bb9fb3a",
      "name": "Section 0 - Sheet Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        1312
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Gmail Trigger / Email Retrieval\nThe Schedule Trigger runs the workflow at predefined intervals (every minute) to poll the Gmail inbox. \"Get many messages\" retrieves incoming messages in full form, including any attachments, so they can be processed downstream.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b226d17e-33c9-4f7f-8590-fe93900910e0",
      "name": "Section 1 - Email Retrieval",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        720,
        1056
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Label Detection / Handling\nThe Code node maps each message's Gmail label IDs to a readable label name (Inquiries, Applications, Documents) and extracts sender, subject, date, and attachment details. Emails without a recognised label fall back to \"Unlabeled\" throughout the workflow.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "ce764a6c-5709-466a-9305-9916f5c040e5",
      "name": "Section 2 - Label Detection",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        976,
        1568
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Deduplication\nEach Gmail Message ID is checked against the \"processed_emails\" data table. \"Skip if already processed\" only passes messages not seen before, and the Message ID is recorded after processing. This prevents duplicate processing, duplicate Sheet rows, and duplicate Drive uploads. \"Has attachment?\" then routes emails with attachments to the Drive/logging path and those without to a simpler logging path.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "28e2e57c-32c0-4081-b32d-6c0743c84746",
      "name": "Section 3 - Deduplication",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1408,
        1568
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Folder Management\nThe workflow builds the Google Drive hierarchy Label -> Date Received -> Sender. For each level it first searches for an existing folder (\"Search label folder\", \"Search date folder\") and reuses it when found; if it does not exist, the matching \"Create ... folder\" node creates it. The resulting folder IDs are stored (Set Label/Date ID) for the next level.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 404,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "1a6b36d9-b80b-4f96-9793-6cf9788dbda2",
      "name": "Section 4 - Folder Management",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2720,
        1616
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Sender Folder Matching\nSender folders are matched with an exact name query scoped to the correct Date folder (name = sender AND parent = date folder). This ensures different sender names do not accidentally share a folder. If no exact match exists, \"Create sender folder\" creates it and the folder ID is stored in \"Set Sender ID\".",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "45396200-bf2d-4305-91a5-93101d5873ed",
      "name": "Section 5 - Sender Folder Matching",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3552,
        1200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6. Attachment Handling\n\"Attach binary\" re-attaches the original attachment binary to the current item, and \"Upload file\" uploads it into the matched sender folder while preserving the original filename.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "4b06d304-bc67-4640-a6e7-479cff2bafe0",
      "name": "Section 6 - Attachment Handling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4592,
        1216
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 7. Google Sheets Logging\nProcessing results are logged to the Google Sheet. \"Append row with links\" records emails with attachments, including a HYPERLINK to the Drive sender folder, while \"Append row in sheet\" logs emails without attachments. Both capture date, label, subject, sender, status, and processing time.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "68bc02bb-5a1a-4cd7-9632-cae5e27c3be2",
      "name": "Section 7 - Sheets Logging",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1632,
        1008
      ]
    }
  ],
